WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.560
Once you've initialized Tessle in your

2
00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:06.960
project, it's recommended that you

3
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.360
integrate Tessle with your preferred AI

4
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.840
coding agent. In this video, we'll show

5
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.840
you how to connect Tessle with Gemini

6
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.080
CLI.

7
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.439
At a terminal, from within your project

8
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.880
route, run Tessle setup agent. This will

9
00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:23.680
give you a list of agents you can pick

10
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.760
from. We'll select Gemini CLI and let

11
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.080
Tesla auto configure the MCP

12
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.960
integration. That's it. Now when I run

13
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.800
Gemini CLI, it picks up the Tessle MCP

14
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.800
server straight away and is ready to

15
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.880
use.

16
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:41.120
You've now got Tessle connected as an

17
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:43.360
MCP server within Gemini CLI. Your next

18
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.879
step is to use the spec registry or

19
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.879
Tessle framework.
